# ─── App config (baked into the bundle at build time) ──────────────────────

# Centralized claims service (ar-io-claims) base URL. REQUIRED — this is the
# only backend the app talks to. Every lookup and claim goes through it: it
# holds the escrowed assets, issues the canonical message to sign, verifies the
# recipient signature, and dispenses to the claimant's Solana wallet. Point it
# at your deployment (local dev default shown). The claim page surfaces a banner
# if it is unset or unreachable. The settings menu overrides + persists this.
VITE_CLAIMS_API_URL=http://localhost:3040

# Network label bound into the canonical claim message and pinned by the client
# when it re-verifies the server's canonical before signing. Must equal the
# claims service's own NETWORK. Otherwise inferred from VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL.
# solana-mainnet | solana-devnet.
# VITE_ESCROW_NETWORK=solana-mainnet

# Solana RPC endpoint. Used ONLY to (a) infer the network label above and (b)
# back the optional Solana wallet connection that auto-fills the claim
# destination address. No transactions are ever built or sent from the browser —
# the claims service dispenses on-chain. Defaults to mainnet-beta.
VITE_SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com

# ─── Deploy (yarn deploy → permaweb-deploy) ────────────────────────────────

# ArNS name to assign the deployed manifest to (you must own it on AR.IO).
VITE_ARNS_NAME=my-escrow-app

# Arweave deploy wallet, base64-encoded JWK. Set at deploy time only — never
# commit it. Generate with:  export DEPLOY_KEY=$(base64 -i wallet.json)
# (Alternatively pass --wallet ./wallet.json or --private-key to permaweb-deploy.)
# DEPLOY_KEY=
